course: dictionary
lesson: 12399
title: Right now: currently
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Currently means now, at this time. It tells you how things are at the moment, and they may change later.
explain: «The shop is currently closed.» The word currently tells you the shop is shut right now. It may open later, so the situation can change.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in now. «The shop is now closed» still makes sense, so currently means now here.
fact: Currently means now, at this time.
fact: It tells how things are at the moment, and things may change later.
fact: «The library is currently open until five o'clock.» means the library is open at this moment.
fact: In maths, a currently amount is the starting amount, before anything changes in the problem.
fact: In science, what we currently know may change when new discoveries are made.
exercise: «The bus is currently at the station.» What does currently mean here? | *At this moment | Never again | Next week | Long ago
exercise: Sam currently has 12 stickers, then he buys 5 more. What is the starting amount? | 7 | *12 | 17 | 5
exercise: Scientists say what we currently know about dinosaurs may change. Why? | Because scientists stop looking | *Because new discoveries can change what we know | Because the facts are always the same forever | Because dinosaurs are alive again
test: «The café is currently full, so please wait.» What does currently tell you? | The café was full last year and never again | The café is always full | *The café is full right now | The café will be full every day
test: Ella says currently means forever. Is she right? | No, it means yesterday | Yes, it means forever | *No, it means now, and things may change later | Yes, it means it never changes
exam: Which word means the same as now, at this time? | Always | *Currently | Recently | Eventually
